  "source_finding": "The drawings reverse the CGW-to-camera/radar order: the Camry comparison has CGW -> radar -> FRC, Corolla has CGW -> FRC -> radar. The shared 9/10 repin splits the camera-radar connection in both. Corolla FRC retains its 1/2 connection toward CGW through untouched harness passthroughs.",
  "inference": "The untouched gateway-facing 1/2 connection is a candidate for alternate reachability, not an established packet-path explanation. No inspected source establishes forwarding between FRC interfaces 1/2 and 9/10 for the control/signing messages. Camera/radar attachment order does not explain a clean native-source reversal by itself.",
  "unresolved": [
    "The drawings expose external connections, not the electrical implementation or packet forwarding inside the camera/radar.",
    "The Toyota Bus-1 camera/radar attachment order has not been joined to the exact end-to-end SecOC packet path; the supplied Camry overview draws Toyota Bus 4 separately with CGW/EPS termination.",
    "GTS+ CAN Bus Check is not a packet-by-packet routing matrix; the source-to-interface paths for 0x030, 0x081, 0x777, 0x7A9 and 0x08A remain unresolved.",
    "No new live bus capture, continuity measurement, or PCS handoff test was performed."
  ],
  "integration_implication": "Blocking only the 9/10 FRC->radar path does not establish isolation of FRC 0x08A from its untouched 1/2 gateway-facing path. Reversing bus constants alone is not a source-isolation proof.",
